Skill add_ai_task_delivery {
  label: 'Add delivery to an AI task'
  description: "Use when an AI task's result should be sent by email or to Slack, for a new task, this chat's draft, or a task the user names. Always settles the destination and the attachment. Typical phrasings: “email me the summary every Friday”, “post it in #sales-alerts”, “attach the chart”. Loaded by create_ai_task whenever the destination is email or Slack. Do not load it for a send right now, or when the result only stays in Holistics."
  invocation: 'auto'
  disabled: H.git.is_production
  content: @md
    # Add delivery to an AI task

    Settle who gets the task's result and what comes with it, then write it into the task's brief. A scheduled run sends on its own: add no disclaimer about sending.

    ## Destination

    - **Settled:** a named email address, a Slack channel, or "email me" (the signed-in user, `${H.current_user.h_email}`). Don't ask again.
    - **Email to a group or team:** ask "Which email addresses? Type them." No recommendation.
    - **Slack:** ask "Which Slack channel? Type its exact name." No recommendation; if the user can't name one, ask again or offer email. Never fill a missing channel with one from another task.
    - **Several destinations** are fine; write each one.

    ## Attachment (always ask)

    Whenever the result is sent, ask one `ask_user` card, even when the request says nothing about an attachment. Skip it only when the user already named one or said none.
    - "What should come with the result?" with "A chart of the result (recommended)", "The <name> dashboard" and "No attachment".
    - For the dashboard option, look for a dashboard on the task's data (`*.page.aml`, every folder level) and name the best match. If none fits, offer "A dashboard (tell me which)".
    - A file type the user names ("as a PDF") is settled: write it as the Attachment.
    - Keep the best pick of the other kind for the draft report's button: for a chart, a dashboard you found ("Attach the <name> dashboard instead"); for a dashboard, "Attach a chart instead". No button when nothing is attached.

    ## Write it into the brief

    - **At a glance:** Sends to = each destination ("Email · you@x.com", "Slack · #sales", joined by "; "); Condition = the rule in plain words when sending only on a condition; Attachment = "None", "Viz · PNG", "Dashboard · <name> · PNG" or the file type.
    - **Steps:** add or fill the {Condition} step (when it sends: exclusive branches, each naming its destinations; it never writes the message), the {Attach} step (export the chart or dashboard as PNG) and the {Deliver} step (send one message to each destination with the attachment).
    - **Subject:** in the {Deliver} step write the subject word for word: email "<task label> · <this period's dates>" (digits, for example "Mar 4 – 10"; no period for a task without one), Slack "<task label>". Never a word like "Last Week" in place of the dates.
    - Add an acceptance criterion only if the destination or condition changes what a run must produce.
  ;;
}
